+- **Distinguish** two separate ledgers: (i) hard safety budget charging conservative all-host CPU upper bounds and accumulating them across every authorized trial unless Economy makes a new explicit appropriation; (ii) empirical attribution/value accounting, where actual per-office CPU remains UNAVAILABLE until independently metered, never imputed from host activity.
+- The UPPER_BOUND whole-host CPU charging is a safety mechanism applicable **only** during the first bounded Statistics trial. It does not establish a resource accounting precedent for subsequent trials.
+- UPPER_BOUND charges across trials must be independently tracked and not aggregated for disabling or capping purposes.
